# gate/treesitter.baseline — the exact disagreement between the two grammar
# authorities, pinned so that a SEVENTEENTH cannot arrive quietly.
#
# Produced by `idol run gate/treesitter.id`, which reads the owner's generated
# role table, src/lexer.zig's spelling map, and ext/tree-sitter-idol/grammar.js
# — three producers, no restated fact. Every line below is a place where the
# authored editor grammar and lib/compiler/token.id say different things about
# the SAME operator.
#
# A RATCHET, NOT A BUDGET. The gate fails when a divergence appears that is not
# here, AND when a line here no longer describes a divergence. Fixing one means
# deleting its line in the same diff.
#
# WHY THESE CANNOT BE FIXED IN PLACE. grammar.js is generated by
# scripts/treesitter_emit.id, which does not run: it reaches
# `method-unresolved:split` in the direct-native backend, and its operator
# ladder is cross-checked against a numbered precedence section of
# docs/spec/grammar.md that no longer exists, so it would refuse with
# "yielded 0 precedence rows" even once it lowered. Hand-editing a generated
# file is not an option. GAP-134 carries the ordered repair.

# ── 7 comparisons: the owner says NONASSOC, tree-sitter says LEFT.
# `a < b < c` is refused by the compiler and accepted by the editor grammar.
assoc in nonassoc left
assoc < nonassoc left
assoc > nonassoc left
assoc == nonassoc left
assoc != nonassoc left
assoc <= nonassoc left
assoc >= nonassoc left

# ── concat: the owner says RIGHT, tree-sitter says LEFT.
assoc .. right left

# ── infix `@` (matmul) exists for the compiler and not for the editor.
missing @

# ── `~=` is recognized by the editor grammar as an operator the owner does
# not own. src/grammar_roles.zig records that this spelling moved to xor-assign.
extra ~=

# ── 6 induced-order disagreements. All of them are `..` and `~` sitting in
# the wrong band: the owner puts `..` between `+ -` and `<< >>`, the editor
# grammar puts it between `&` and the comparisons, and the owner separates
# `~` from `|` where the editor grammar ties them.
order & ..
order | ~
order | ..
order ~ ..
order .. <<
order .. >>
